  "description": "Techniques around the 2016 to 2017 NSA and CIA tool leaks: the Equation group as ATT&CK records it, the WannaCry and NotPetya malware that reused the leaked SMBv1 exploits, the NotPetya supply-chain vector, and this study's inferred mapping of the Vault 7 insider theft and the Hive tool; not an official MITRE mapping. Sources: ATT&CK G0020, S0366, S0368, S0606 and T1210 as published in ATT&CK v20, CISA TA17-132A and TA17-181A, Microsoft's 2017 analyses, the SDNY court record, the CIA WikiLeaks Task Force report and WikiLeaks' Vault 8 page. Tactics are taken from data/attack/technique_profiles.jsonl. Scores: 100 an ATT&CK object maps the technique, 70 an advisory describes the behavior and the study assigns the id, 40 the mapping is Inferred. Each comment names source numbers from the Sources table of case-studies/NSA_CIA_TOOL_LEAKS.md.",
